  "content": {
    "id": "p6-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "A boat builder needs to calculate the lengths of the stays needed to support a mast on a yacht. Two of the stays ($AB$ and $AD$) will be the same length, as they go from a point $A$ on the mast to each side of the boat, as shown in the diagram. The third stay ($AE$) will be different in length as it goes from the point $A$ on the mast to the front of the boat.\n\nIf $AC=5\\text{ m}$, $CB=CD=1.2\\text{ m}$ and $CE=1.9\\text{ m}$, find the length, to the nearest centimetre, of:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p6-q10-front",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "\\begin{tikzpicture}[line join=round,line width=0.8pt,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont]\n\\coordinate(A)at(0,2.5);\\coordinate(C)at(0,0);\\coordinate(D)at(-.9,0);\\coordinate(B)at(.9,0);\n\\draw[black](A)--(D)--(B)--cycle;\\draw[black](A)--(0,-.55);\\draw[black](D)..controls(-.7,-.5)and(-.25,-.2)..(0,-.55)..controls(.25,-.2)and(.7,-.5)..(B);\n\\draw[black,line width=.4pt](0,.12)--(.12,.12)--(.12,0);\n\\node[above]at(A){$A$};\\node[above right]at(C){$C$};\\node[left]at(D){$D$};\\node[right]at(B){$B$};\\node[below]at(0,-.75){Front elevation};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 48,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 6,
          "description": "Front elevation: mastAC vertical above deckDCB; staysAD/AB; rightangle atC; simple native hull context retained. D,C,B collinear; no dimension invented.",
          "sizing": {
            "exceptionReason": "Meaningful elevation caption and all necessary A/B/C/D labels retained at10pt; width48mm allows the full caption."
          }
        },
        "derived": false,
        "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q10-side",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "\\begin{tikzpicture}[line join=round,line width=0.8pt,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont]\n\\coordinate(A)at(0,2.5);\\coordinate(C)at(0,0);\\coordinate(E)at(1.5,0);\n\\draw[black](A)--(E)--(-1,0);\\draw[black](A)--(0,-.55);\\draw[black](-1,0)..controls(-.9,-.65)and(.7,-.65)..(E);\n\\draw[black,line width=.4pt](0,.12)--(.12,.12)--(.12,0);\n\\node[above]at(A){$A$};\\node[above left]at(C){$C$};\\node[right]at(E){$E$};\\node[below]at(.25,-.75){Side elevation};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 48,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 6,
          "description": "Side elevation: mastAC vertical, deckCE horizontal, front stayAE, rightangle atC; mast continues below deck and simple native hull retained.",
          "sizing": {
            "exceptionReason": "Paired elevation caption and necessary A/C/E labels at10pt; keep common mast height and scale with front elevation."
          }
        },
        "derived": false,
        "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
      }
    ],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p6-q10-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "one of the side stays, $AB$ or $AD$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5.14\\text{ m}$",
          "worked": "In right-angled triangle $ACB$:\n$$\\begin{align*}AB^2&=5^2+1.2^2\\\\AB^2&=26.44\\\\AB&=\\sqrt{26.44}\\text{ m}\\\\AB&\\approx5.14\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$\nThe other side stay has the same length. To the nearest centimetre, each is $5.14\\text{ m}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 68
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q10-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "the front stay, $AE$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5.35\\text{ m}$",
          "worked": "In right-angled triangle $ACE$:\n$$\\begin{align*}AE^2&=5^2+1.9^2\\\\AE^2&=28.61\\\\AE&=\\sqrt{28.61}\\text{ m}\\\\AE&\\approx5.35\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$\nThe front stay is $5.35\\text{ m}$ long, to the nearest centimetre.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      },
      {
        "id": "p6-q10-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "stainless steel wire needed to make the three stays",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$15.63\\text{ m}$\n\nAdd the three unrounded lengths before rounding.",
          "worked": "Add both side stays and the front stay, retaining the unrounded roots:\n$$\\begin{align*}L&=AB+AD+AE\\\\L&=2\\sqrt{26.44}+\\sqrt{28.61}\\\\L&\\approx15.63\\text{ m}\\end{align*}$$\nThe three stays require $15.63\\text{ m}$ of wire, to the nearest centimetre.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 60
      }
    ]
  },
